lse,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124073","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124073.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124073.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15590 by providing a non-compatibility-breaking solution.\r\n- Related: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/issues/12414\r\n\r\nThis PR adds new and more descriptive joypad paddle button constants and deprecates the old ones:\r\n- `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE1` -> `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE_RIGHT1`\r\n- `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE2` -> `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE_LEFT1`\r\n- `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE3` -> `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE_RIGHT2`\r\n- `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE4` -> `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE_LEFT2`\r\n\r\nThis PR uses paddle numbers instead of up/down paddles in case in the future we may need to add new paddle constants (for example, `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE_RIGHT3` and `JOY_BUTTON_PADDLE_LEFT3`).\r\n\r\nPlease let me know your opinion on the issue and this solution!","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124073/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124073/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}